Z||000000||grinthock||08-14-2001||10:34 PM||||Well after confirming that my IAC pintle IS moving properly I am starting to think EGR, ocasinally the car wants to DIE, like it's choking or something, could my EGR be sticking in the OPEN position, I know it's something flakey cause it's only occsaionally and when it doesnt happen the car runs GREAT.....  How can I check the egr valve?  My understanding is that the car will NOT throw a code if the EGR is stuck in the OPEN state only if it sticks closed||||reg||1
Z||000001||grinthock||08-15-2001||10:29 AM||||Sometimes posts get lost in busy hours...<P><BR>Anyone?||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||08-16-2001||01:13 AM||||You can move the EGR plunger by hand to see if it retracts back to the 'off' position.  Of course, do this with the car cold for obvious reasons. GL||||reg||1
Z||000003||falconhulk||08-23-2001||09:02 AM||||I have a problem similar to this.  Its only when slowing down after driving for a prolonged period.  Whenb this happens my Check Engine light lights though!  Is this what happens when the EGR sticks?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/i-4_b_l.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||grinthock||08-24-2001||07:21 PM||||Just an update.<P>Found the following<P>plugs are kinda yucky<BR>Wires Suck<BR>Cap has rust<BR>EGR tube Clogged<BR>EGR Valve Weak.<P><BR>Lots to do!  Got the new plugs done at least... Bosch +4's||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||08-24-2001||11:37 PM||||Fix all of that and see how it runs.  Sounds to me like a good tune up will go a long way to fixing the problem.  You may also want to check all the vacumn lines for leakes.  They break easily, and will cause lots ofproblems if they do!<P>I spent a lot of time and money tracking down a stalling problem.  Finally one day, while looking over the engine, I noticed a broken vacumn tube elbow going into the throttle body.  Fixing this also fixed my problem!||||reg||1
